# SFT execution status v0.113

2026-09-26. The dropped-worker final-seal, SCM_RIGHTS transfer,
parent-reservation ledger and sealed READY/release/CONSUMED protocol candidates
are implemented, hardened and locally verified. **This is still not an
integrated native write guard; Gate 5 remains incomplete.** No checkpoint,
tokenizer or dataset payload was read. No child process, native filter,
listener transfer, socket transaction, ioctl, pidfd, cgroup, worker, remote
mutation, GPU operation, inference or training occurred. The eleven successor
files remain local and unpushed.

## Completed

- A real ordering bug was fixed without modifying listener v1: root preparation
  and transfer remain frozen, while the v2 final seal now requires the same
  process and main thread after exact irreversible uid/gid 10001 transition,
  empty supplementary groups, no-new-privileges and inherited listener filter.
- The private transfer candidate validates one borrowed root-owned connected
  local seqpacket channel and performs one digest-bound SCM_RIGHTS offer/ACK.
  Ownership transfer is explicit. Malformed rights, including an unexpected
  SCM_PIDFD, are retired; descriptor reuse and nonzero receive flags fail
  closed. Socket metadata still does not prove process origin or exclusivity.
- Before each CONTINUE, the broker proposes one aggregate ordinal, requested
  byte count and cumulative reservation. The parent validates and stores that
  conservative upper bound before attempting its acknowledgement. Later ACK,
  ID-validation, response or broker failure cannot refund the reservation.
- Worker control uses two separate precreated channels. READY and CONSUMED use
  the report channel; the guardian's one-byte release and close use the release
  channel. This permits the worker to close the release FD before acknowledging
  consumption on the still-open report FD.
- Post-seal reads, writes and poll are fixed raw scalar syscalls allowed by the
  frozen filter. Poll does not receive Python's implicit EINTR retry. An empty
  read with HUP is recorded only as that observation—not as queue-drain proof.
- All public entries remain closed, all state is one-shot and fail-closed, and
  all retained results are fixed codes or aggregate scalars with unproved
  execution and native-enforcement claims explicitly false.

## Verification

**821 unique tests pass on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with no failures,
errors or skips: 31 listener-v2, 33 transport, 36 ledger, 24 protocol and 697
prior regression tests. The focused 124-test successor suite also passes on
both runtimes. Every native boundary in the new tests is synthetic.

Syntax/AST checks pass for all eight new source/test files on both runtimes;
maximum line length is 100 and trailing whitespace is zero. Tests used `-B`,
and no bytecode file for the new component names is present. Existing unrelated
repository bytecode was intentionally left untouched. Ruff was unavailable and
no replacement was downloaded.

All 10 bindings in the direct predecessor plan match their recorded byte counts
and SHA-256 values. Its 61 earlier recorded bindings were not reread in this
successor. Tracked unstaged and staged diffs remain empty; existing untracked
evidence was preserved.

