## Exact next work and unchanged boundary

The next successor must first version the guardian so cgroup-lease and release
descriptor ownership transfer is unambiguous on every early error. It must then
implement the controller-owned process topology: dedicated broker spawn, exact
inherited-FD close matrix, listener handoff/adoption, worker privilege drop and
seal, READY verification before guardian arming, release consumption,
parent-ledger callbacks, terminal kill handling and pidfd-based broker/worker
reap. Trusted single-writer/no-extra-packet topology must be constructed rather
than inferred from socket metadata.

After that comes integration into the frozen full-size bootstrap, dispatcher
and lifecycle closure; successor source-closure authentication; and a separately
authorized bounded Linux native qualification. Only a passing native
qualification can return to the unchanged host, input, resource and real-import
admission gates. These are remaining parts of Gate 5, not new roadmap gates.

GPU is not needed for the next local guardian/composition work. The S3-backed
pretrained checkpoint remains the intended base, but no current remote
availability check was made. Real import, training and production remain
disabled.
